\f1\fs22 The rest of the day passed almost wordlessly, with the three of them seeking out separate spaces in their five-star jailhouse: outdoor nooks under dappled sunlight; luxurious divans in front of unlit fireplaces; dining tables made of almost extinct timbers, ideal for resting tablets on while they swiped and read; upstairs studies with glimpses through the trees of the valley beyond. They grazed on fruit and baked goods, brewed teas and coffees at independent times, and generally tried to stay the hell away from each other. Around mid-afternoon there was a succession of knocks at the door\'97some valet-type person delivering personal items retrieved from each of the three\'92s homes. Kathy was relieved when she found her delivery included an almost adequate supply of patches.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 At separate dinner times determined by separate stomachs, they found pre-made curries and pasta dishes in the stasis fridge. Or at least Hayley and Sarah did; Kathy promised the others she wouldn\'92t go back in there without adult supervision. She defiantly declared she wasn\'92t hungry anyway, cracked open the oldest, most expensive-looking Coonawarra red from the cellar and drank it straight from the bottle.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Sarah announced she was going to bed, and warned Kathy not to raid the fridge overnight.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93How are you gonna stop me?\'94 Kathy challenged.\
\'93I\'92ll sleep in your bed, if I have to,\'94 Sarah replied. Kathy had moved out of Sarah\'92s bedroom involving a snoring incident and a wrongly accused lyrebird nesting just beyond the yard fence.\
\'93Oooh, really?\'94 Kathy clapped her hands.\
Later, when they were both between the same sheets\'97Kathy vibrantly naked\'97Sarah said, \'93You know, you\'92re in the wrong bed.\'94\
\'93This is my bed, remember.\'94\
\'93No. I mean\'85 Hayley\'85\'94 Sarah completed her sentence by semaphore of eyebrows and chin movements.\
\'93What about her?\'94\
\'93She\'92s got the smokin\'92 hots for you.\'94\
\'93What?\'94\
\'93Are you telling me you haven\'92t noticed the way she goes all Bambi eyes when she looks at you?\'94\
\'93You mean she wants to pin Bambi\'92s mother\'92s murder on me?\'94\
\'93She likes you.\'94\
\'93That\'92s what I\'92m saying. She likes me for the Bambi mother killing.\'94\
\'93Stop being dense. You have noticed it.\'94\
\'93She\'92s a TRAMP.\'94\
\'93So?\'94\
\'93Police and me\'85 aren\'92t the best of friends.\'94\
\'93Well, that\'92s a feather in your cap, in my book.\'94\
\'93Is the feather in my cap or your book?\'94\
\'93Look. Hayley\'92s no ordinary cop. She\'92s not\'85\'94\
\'93Crooked? Stupid? Compensating for a deep-seeded feeling of powerlessness?\'94\
\'93Don\'92t you mean 
\f2\i deep-seated
\f1\i0 ?\'94 Sarah couldn\'92t help but be correct.\
\'93I prefer seeds. You can grow smokable things from them. Which Hayley would probably confiscate.\'94\
Sarah realised she\'92d get nowhere with the idea tonight, but she hoped she\'92d planted a seed of her own for Kathy\'92s thoughts and desires. Kathy snuggled like an innocent school friend at a sleepover, but it still made Sarah uncomfortable. So she decided to watch some music streaming on her tablet, as much for showing Kathy where her attention wasn\'92t. She slipped her buds in and tapped her way to a tube she often watched.\
A grid of thumbnail images infested her screen: all Elvi artists. One caught her attention, so she tapped. It was a music vid built around a staged \'93live\'94 performance. The chyron at the bottom of the screen read, 
\f2\i Are you evolving tonight
\f1\i0 ? by Elvis and the Holy Mommas. The front Elvis was instantly recognisable in a dragon-motif jump suit and sunglasses, but it took a moment to realise what the Elvi in the band were on about, all in formal dresses and wearing long blonde wigs.\
\'93Oh, my god! They\'92re impersonating me!\'94 Sarah blurted, rousing Kathy.\
Worse, as the cameras panned back from the sickening angles of the close-ups, Sarah caught flashes of satin pink, and what appeared to be legs. The vision pulled back for a full-stage shot, too fast for Sarah to register the meaning of it.\
The front Elvis sang:\
